      <div style="margin-top:6pt;margin-left:69.66pt;width:456pt;">
        <div style="width:456pt; line-height:12pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">ended 2022 and 2023, an assumed growth rate of 40% for the fiscal years ended 2024 and 2025, and certain other financial information provided by CXApp management to first calculate estimated unlevered free cash flows, which is defined as non-GAAP adjusted earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization, less taxes and capital expenditures, and adjusted for changes in net working capital. GVS then calculated the present value of unlevered free cash flows for the Enterprise Apps Business for the forecasted period using discount rates ranging from 14.5% to 19.5% which were selected based on GVS&#8217;s professional judgment and experience, to reflect an estimate of CXApp&#8217;s weighted average cost of capital estimated using the capital asset pricing model method and utilizing a normalized risk-free rate of 3.5% and 5.5% market risk premium both recommended by Duff &amp; Phelps (Rebranded as Kroll) for the current period , and a 1.0 predicted beta based on guideline comparable companies and target debt to equity ratio of subject company. GVS then calculated terminal enterprise values at the end of the forecasted period by applying an EV/Revenue multiple to the terminal year revenue estimate. The arrived terminal enterprise values were then discounted to calculate ranges of implied indications of present values using the above discount rates. GVS then added the ranges of the implied present values of the unlevered free cash flows of between $(1.55) million as of FY22 and $5.56 million as of FY25 to the ranges of implied present values of our terminal enterprise values to derive ranges of implied present enterprise value ranging between $61.7&#160;million and $70.3&#160;million for the Enterprise Apps Business. </font>
        </div>
        <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">Below is a summary table of unlevered cash flows calculated in connection with the discounted cash flow analysis. </font>
        </div>
