        <div style="margin-top:12.3pt; width:456pt;">
          <div style="margin-left: 0pt; width: 108pt; margin-top: 0pt; font-size: 1pt; line-height: 0pt; border-bottom: 1pt solid #000000; ">&#8203;</div>
        </div>
        <div style=" float:left; margin-top:7.8pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-align:left; width:20pt;white-space:nowrap;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">(1)</font>
          <br >
        </div>
        <div style=" margin-top:7.8pt; margin-bottom:0pt; line-height:12pt; text-align:left; margin-left:20pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">The projected financial data provided in this table includes non-GAAP financial measures. These non-GAAP financial measures should not be considered as an alternative to operating income or net income as measures of operating performance, or an alternative to cash flows, as a measure of liquidity. They also should not be considered in isolation from, or as a substitute for, financial information presented in accordance with GAAP. CXApp&#8217;s calculation of non-GAAP financial measures may differ from others in its industry and the non-GAAP financial measures in the table are not necessarily comparable with similar titled measures used by other companies. </font>
        </div>
        <div style="clear:both; padding:0pt; margin:0pt;font-size:0pt;line-height:0pt;">&#8203;</div>
        <div style=" float:left; line-height:12pt; margin-top:3.8pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-align:left; width:20pt;white-space:nowrap;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">(2)</font>
          <br >
        </div>
        <div style=" margin-top:3.8pt; margin-bottom:0pt; line-height:12pt; text-align:left; margin-left:20pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">EBITDA is calculated as revenue less cost of revenue and operating expenses including selling, general and administrative (&#8220;SG&amp;A&#8221;) expense. </font>
        </div>
        <div style="clear:both; padding:0pt; margin:0pt;font-size:0pt;line-height:0pt;">&#8203;</div>
        <div style=" float:left; line-height:12pt; margin-top:3.8pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-align:left; width:20pt;white-space:nowrap;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">(3)</font>
          <br >
        </div>
        <div style=" margin-top:3.8pt; margin-bottom:0pt; line-height:12pt; text-align:left; margin-left:20pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">Unlevered free cash flow is calculated as EBITDA, plus depreciation and amortization, less taxes, less capital expenditures, less change in net working capital. </font>
        </div>
        <div style="clear:both; padding:0pt; margin:0pt;font-size:0pt;line-height:0pt;">&#8203;</div>
        <div style="margin-top:12pt; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;font-weight:bold;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:-0.2pt;">Summary of Financial Analyses performed by KNAV.</font><font style="font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:0.2pt;"> </font>
        </div>
        <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:11.5pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">The following is a brief summary of the material analyses performed by KNAV in connection with its opinion letter dated September&#160;23, 2022, to the KINS Board. The following summary is not a complete description of KNAV&#8217;s opinion, the financial analyses performed, and factors considered by KNAV in connection with its opinion, nor does the order of analyses described represent the relative importance or weight given to those analyses. Some of these summaries of financial analyses include information presented in tabular format. To fully understand the financial analyses used by KNAV, the tables must be read together with the text of each summary. The tables alone do not constitute a complete description of the financial analyses. The analyses listed in the tables and described below must be considered as a whole; considering any portion of such analyses and the factors in isolation could create a misleading or incomplete view of the process underlying KNAV&#8217;s opinion. </font>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:12pt; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;font-weight:bold;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:-0.2pt;">Discounted Cash flow (&#8220;DCF&#8221;) Analysis</font><font style="font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:0.2pt;"> </font>
        </div>
        <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:11.5pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">KNAV performed a discounted cash flow analysis, which is designed to provide an implied value of a company by calculating the present value of the estimated future cash flows and terminal value of such a company. KNAV calculated a range of equity values for CXApp utilizing estimates from the Financial Projections for purposes of its discounted cash flow analysis. KNAV first calculated the estimated unlevered free cash flow, which is defined as non-GAAP adjusted earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization, less taxes and capital expenditures, and adjusted for changes in net working capital. The free </font>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:2.00000000000002pt;height:12pt;margin-left:69.66pt;width:456pt;">
        <div style="margin-top:5pt; text-align:center; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">&#160;</font>
          <br >
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:21.86pt;margin-left:69.66pt;width:456pt;">
        <div style="margin-top:5pt; text-align:center; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">166</font>
          <br >
        </div>
      </div>
      <hr >
    </div>
    <div style="page-break-after:always; width:595.3pt;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;font-variant:normal;text-transform:none;color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman, Times, serif ;font-size:10pt;">
      <div style="padding:0pt;margin:0pt;font-family:calibri, arial, sans-serif;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;font-size:8pt;line-height:8pt;">
        <a style="text-decoration:none;color:#003366;" href="#TOC">TABLE OF CONTENTS</a>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:15.85pt;height:24pt;margin-left:69.66pt;width:456pt;">
        <div style="margin-top:17pt; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">&#160;</font>
          <br >
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:6pt;margin-left:69.66pt;width:456pt;">
        <div style="width:456pt; line-height:11.5pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">cash flows and terminal values were discounted to present values as of August 22, 2022, at a discount rate&#160;ranging from 19.56% to 21.06%, which discount rates were selected, upon the application of KNAV&#8217;s professional judgment and experience, to reflect an estimate of CXApp&#8217;s weighted average cost of capital estimated using the capital asset pricing model method and utilizing a risk-free rate of 3.48% based on the 20-year U.S. Treasury yield as of August 22, 2022, 6.22% market risk premium, and a 1.12 predicted beta based on guideline comparable companies and target debt to equity ratio of subject company. It also considered a size-risk premium of 7.89% and a company-specific risk premium of 2.00% considering CXApp&#8217;s sensitivity to current heightened geo-political and macro-economic uncertainty, the discretionary nature of the services provided by the subject company; and high revenue growth and aggressive margin improvement with risk of success aggravated by current cash burn. To calculate terminal values, KNAV utilized perpetual growth rates of 4.95% to 6.45% as part of its analyses, with such rates selected upon the application of KNAV&#8217;s professional judgment and experience. The resulting aggregate value was then adjusted for non-current assets (net) and net cash and further adjusted to add the net present values of tax amortization benefits and tax savings on net operating losses. The resultant equity value range of CXApp, taking into account the closing company adjusted cash, estimated using the discounted cash flow analysis described above is $56,725 thousand &#8211; $66,925 thousand. </font>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:12pt; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;font-weight:bold;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:-0.2pt;">Guideline Public Company (&#8220;GPC) Analysis</font>
        </div>
        <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:11.5pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">KNAV performed a guideline public company analysis, which attempts to provide an implied value of a company by comparing it to similar companies that are publicly traded. KNAV reviewed and compared certain financial estimates for CXApp with comparable publicly available consensus equity analyst research estimates for companies, selected based on KNAV&#8217;s professional judgment and experience, that share&#160;similar business characteristics and have certain comparable operating characteristics including, among other things, similarly sized revenue and/or revenue growth rates, geography of operations, market capitalizations, profitability, scale and/or other similar operating characteristics (these companies are referred to as the &#8220;comparable companies&#8221;). For purposes of this analysis, KNAV analyzed the ratio of aggregate value to actual and estimated revenues, which, for purposes of this analysis, was provided to KNAV, and approved for KNAV&#8217;s use, by KINS&#8217; management for last-twelve month actuals (&#8220;LTM&#8221;) and for next-twelve months (&#8220;NTM&#8221;) and Forward FY+2 (&#8220;FY+2&#8221;) for the Financial Projections for CXApp, and for each of the comparable companies, was based on publicly available consensus equity analyst research estimates for comparison purposes. For purposes of its analyses, KNAV defined &#8220;enterprise value&#8221; as a company&#8217;s market value of invested capital minus cash and short-term investments. </font>
        </div>
        <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:11.5pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">The following is a list of the selected comparable companies reviewed, together with the applicable multiples: </font>
        </div>
