        <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:7.9pt; width:456pt; line-height:11.5pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">Based on its analysis of the relevant metrics for each of the comparable companies and upon the application of its professional judgment and experience, KNAV selected representative ranges of enterprise value to revenue multiples of 4.98x to 5.98x, 4.39x to 5.39x and 3.88x to 4.88x for LTM, NTM and FY+2, </font>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:2.00000000000002pt;height:12pt;margin-left:69.66pt;width:456pt;">
        <div style="margin-top:5pt; text-align:center; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">&#160;</font>
          <br >
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:2pt;margin-bottom:21.86pt;margin-left:69.66pt;width:456pt;">
        <div style="margin-top:5pt; text-align:center; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">167</font>
          <br >
        </div>
      </div>
      <hr >
    </div>
    <div style="page-break-after:always; width:595.3pt;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;font-variant:normal;text-transform:none;color:#000000;font-family:Times New Roman, Times, serif ;font-size:10pt;">
      <div style="padding:0pt;margin:0pt;font-family:calibri, arial, sans-serif;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;font-size:8pt;line-height:8pt;">
        <a style="text-decoration:none;color:#003366;" href="#TOC">TABLE OF CONTENTS</a>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:15.85pt;height:24pt;margin-left:69.66pt;width:456pt;">
        <div style="margin-top:17pt; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">&#160;</font>
          <br >
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:6pt;margin-left:69.66pt;width:456pt;">
        <div style="width:456pt; line-height:11.5pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">respectively. KNAV then applied these ranges of multiples to the actual and estimated relevant revenue metric for CXApp. For purposes of this analysis, KNAV utilized publicly available financial information, available as of August&#160;22, 2022. </font>
        </div>
        <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:11.5pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">Considering the results of the GPC analysis, KNAV applied the resultant multiple ranges to therespective revenue matrix for CXApp. The resultant equity value range of CXApp, taking into accountthe Closing Company Adjusted Cash, estimated using the GPC analysis described above is $61,192 thousand &#8211; $73,066 thousand. </font>
        </div>
        <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:11.5pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">No company utilized in the guideline public company analysis is identical to CXApp. In evaluating the comparable companies, KNAV made numerous assumptions with respect to industry performance, general business, regulatory, economic, market and financial conditions and other matters, many of which are beyond KINS&#8217; control. These include, among other things, the impact of competition on CXApp&#8217;s business and the industry generally, industry growth, and the absence of any adverse material change in the financial condition and prospects of CXApp and the industry, and in the financial markets in general. Mathematical analysis (such as determining the average or median) is not in itself a meaningful method of using comparable company data.</font>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:12pt; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;font-weight:bold;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:-0.2pt;">Guideline Transactions Analysis</font><font style="font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:0.2pt;"> </font>
        </div>
        <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:11.5pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">KNAV performed a precedent guideline transactions analysis, which is designed to imply a value of a company based on publicly available financial terms. KNAV compared publicly available statistics for selected comparable transactions. KNAV selected such comparable transactions based on its professional judgment and experience. For such transactions, KNAV noted the multiple of enterprise value of the transaction to the last twelve months (&#8220;LTM&#8221;) revenue based on publicly available information at the time of announcement or at the unaffected date of each such transaction. </font>
        </div>
        <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">The following is a list of the selected transactions reviewed, together with the applicable multiples: </font>
