        <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:12pt; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">Transfers to/from Levels 1, 2 and 3 are recognized at the end of the reporting period in which a change in valuation technique or methodology occurs. The estimated fair value of the Public Warrants transferred from a Level&#160;3 measurement to a Level&#160;1 fair value measurement during the three and nine&#160;months ended September&#160;30, 2021 was approximately $9.0&#160;million, when the Public Warrants were separately listed and traded and approximately $6.7&#160;million was transferred from a level 3 to a level 2 fair value measurement. There were no transfers during the three and nine&#160;months ended September&#160;30, 2022. </font>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:12pt; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;font-weight:bold;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:-0.2pt;">NOTE 10.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;SUBSEQUENT EVENTS</font><font style="font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:0.2pt;"> </font>
        </div>
        <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">The Company evaluated subsequent events and transactions that occurred after the September&#160;30, 2022 up to the date that the condensed financial statements were issued. Based upon this review, the Company did not identify any subsequent events that would have required adjustment or disclosure in the condensed financial statements.</font>
        </div>
